---
version: 2.0.2
title: rules: discarded_result reports a discarded prelude result
file: ./test/grice/rules_test.gleam
test_name: discarded_result_reports_a_discarded_prelude_result_test
---
-- src/app.gleam
fn parse() -> Result(Int, Nil) {
  Ok(1)
}

pub fn main() {
  let _ = parse()
  let _ = 1
  let _ = Ok("two")
  Nil
}

// girard can't type this function, and neither could the compiler.
pub fn skipped() {
  let _ = parse()
  1 + "one"
}
-- output
warning[fixture/discarded-result]: Result discarded
  ┌─ src/app.gleam:6:3
  │
6 │   let _ = parse()
  │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This discards a `Result`

A `Result` says whether something failed, and discarding it hides the
failure.

Hint: Handle the error, or assert that there is none.

warning[fixture/discarded-result]: Result discarded
  ┌─ src/app.gleam:8:3
  │
8 │   let _ = Ok("two")
  │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This discards a `Result`

A `Result` says whether something failed, and discarding it hides the
failure.

Hint: Handle the error, or assert that there is none.

note[grice/untyped-definition]: Can't infer the types of this definition
   ┌─ src/app.gleam:13:1
   │
13 │ pub fn skipped() {
   │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ girard couldn't type this definition

girard couldn't type `skipped`: type mismatch: Int vs String. Typed rules
get no answers about the code inside it, so they may miss problems there.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts this code, it's a gap in girard, the type
inference grice uses, so please report it at
https://github.com/alvivi/girard/issues.

2 warnings and 1 note in 1 module.
Coverage is incomplete: 1 definition in 1 module couldn't be typed, so
typed rules didn't see all of the code.

